/review-process-update/\"},{\"title\":\"Large language models for abstract screening in systematic- and scoping reviews: A diagnostic test accuracy study\",\"url\":\"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.10.01.24314702.full.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process/\"},{\"title\":\"Ranking versus rating in peer review of research grant applications\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10553257/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Are numerical scores important for grant assessment? A cross-sectional study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11362741/\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I can provide you with information about the AAAI review process for 2025-2026, though the specific detailed rating scale definitions were not fully available in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## AAAI-26 Review Process Overview\n\nEvery paper will be allocated three reviewers. If a paper receives sufficiently negative reviews, it will be rejected without any opportunity for author feedback. Remaining papers will progress to Phase 2.\n\nAAAI-26 will follow a two-phase reviewing process as in previous years, with two additions: an additional AI-generated review in Phase 1, and an AI-generated review in Phase 2.\n\n## Key Timeline and Deadlines\n\nThe Main Conference Timetable includes: July 25, 2025 for abstracts due; August 1, 2025 for full papers due; October 7-13, 2025 for author feedback window; and November 8, 2025 for notification of final acceptance or rejection (Main Technical Track).\n\n## Review Rating Scale\n\nFrom the available information, researchers reported cases where papers with average scores of 5.5–6.5 were rejected, and even submissions scoring as high as 6.7 did not make the cut in AAAI 2026, suggesting the review scale likely uses numerical scores in a range that includes these values.\n\nThe search results indicate that AAAI uses numerical rating scales, but the complete detailed definitions for each rating category (e.g., what specifically constitutes a score of 5, 6, 7, etc.) were not explicitly provided in the available sources. For the most detailed and accurate rating scale criteria, I recommend consulting the official AAAI-26 reviewer instructions directly on the AAAI website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e048c7cb-c26e-4a6a-9302-1c61fd6549ca","uuid":"64fa4e26-4269-4524-bb5f-247de6d0e12b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:43:53.272Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"AAAI conference paper review criteria rating scale 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019fSahZ39eLThEQkF6UDj7f","content":[{"title":"🔥 Gearing Up for AAAI 2026: What You Need to Know to Win the Game | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/47/gearing-up-for-aaai-2026-what-you-need-to-know-to-win-the-game"},{"title":"AAAI-26 Review Process Update: Scale, Integrity Measures, and Pathways to Sustainability - AAAI","url":"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process-update/"},{"title":"Ethical Guidelines for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI","url":"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/ethical-guidelines-for-aaai-26-reviewers/"},{"title":"ReviewerToo: Should AI Join The Program Committee? A Look At The Future of Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.08867v1"},{"title":"AI-Assisted Peer Review at Scale: The AAAI-26 AI Review Pilot","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.13940v1"},{"title":"AAAI-26 Review Process - AAAI","url":"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process/"},{"title":"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI","url":"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/"}]},"Let me search more specifically